Z||000001||SLYGUY||11-03-2001||01:07 PM||||My quarter windows are trashed too. The passenger side is 'spider' cracked all throughout. The driver's side has a long 8 inch crack in it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I'm gonna go with OEM when I find them. The Fiero Store has them but they are REAL expensive. I'd do it anyways, but I think the clutch is gonna be of more importance right now. Throwout bearing singing a little.<P>If you feel up to it try to find some glass polish or something to try to buff out the scratches. That should help and will be much less expensive than replacing windows entirely.<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rick 88||11-03-2001||06:55 PM||||I can recommend the tinted quarter windows from the Fiero Warehouse. I wanted my quarterwindows to match my tinted side windows. Doug's windows look really great and are about $200.00 for the pair. They give the car a really nice look.<P>Rick 88||||reg||14
Z||000003||avengador1||11-03-2001||07:35 PM||||If you can pas a fingernail over the scratches, without it getting caught, you should be able to polish them out. This is only good for the glass windows. Hope this helps. J.C.Whitney sells the polishing kit if you need one.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
